WEBVTT

00:01:28.138 --> 00:01:30.338
like HPV 6 and 11–

00:01:30.338 --> 00:01:33.588
cause abnormalities in the cells of the 
infected tissue,

00:01:33.588 --> 00:01:36.228
which can develop into genital warts.

00:01:36.228 --> 00:01:39.148
While these are infectious 
and require treatment,

00:01:39.148 --> 00:01:41.068
usually with topical creams,

00:01:41.068 --> 00:01:45.068
wart-causing strains don’t create 
longer-term damage.

00:01:45.068 --> 00:01:49.788
But another 13 strains can cause DNA
mutations that cause cells to divide

00:01:49.788 --> 00:01:52.033
at a much faster pace than normal,

00:01:52.033 --> 00:01:55.033
propelling the development of 
cancerous growths.

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:57.863
The cells of the cervix are 
especially at risks.

00:01:57.863 --> 00:01:59.133
Two in particular–

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.393
HPV 16 and 18–